§6.1: `field.specs.*` **moves** a position to a public field of the author's own.
The entry below assigns all five, so every content lands exactly where it was put
— no `class` / `id` / `style` rename (§6.3 rule 1) and no default path left
behind (§6.1):

[Moved](/pricing)@@moveA{`price_slug`, "Price Title", .price-detail, #john-foo, style: "--width: 200px"}

The same item kinds on an entry that assigns nothing keep the default paths:
`class` / `id` / `style` are the DOM fields they name (§6.3), and the anchor reads
the tick as its id fallback (§6.2) and the quote as its `title`:

[Kept](/docs)@@anchorZ{`slug-a`, "Docs Title", .cta, #main, style: "--tone: red"}

A moved position is the author's own field, so an element does not read it:
`moveA`'s tick is a plain `slug` attribute and never an id, while the unclaimed
type still falls back to it:

[Fallback](/x)@@anchorZ{`slug-b`}
